              "payload": {
                "text": "The refraction of water waves can be further observed if the boundary between the deep and shallow regions is at a certain angle to the incident wavefronts. In this case the deep region acts as the first medium while the shallow region acts as the second medium. If in Activity 1.2, the glass plate was placed at some angle, water waves would be refracted as shown in Figure 1.19.",
